**Convention 11.2 (source-verified primary correspondences).** The
following citations attest only the stated intermediates and
comparison hypotheses. None supplies the missing optimizer equality.

| Primary source | Correspondence and applicability limit |
| --- | --- |
| Guruswami–Riazanov, *Beating Fredman–Komlós for perfect $k$-hashing*, [arXiv:1805.04151v1, §1][GR] | Defines a $k$-hash or $k$-separated code by a coordinate displaying distinct symbols on every $k$ rows. This is Definition 6.3 at $k=4$. Its asymptotic hash-rate bounds are not transferred to the native rate. Proposition 7.1 independently proves the binary family used here. |
| Madiman–Tetali, *Information Inequalities for Joint Distributions, with Interpretations and Applications*, [arXiv:0901.0044v2, Proposition II][MT] | Finite common-law fractional entropy bounds use the same chain-rule and conditioning principles as Lemma 3.1. The additional boundary-vector inequality is proved here; no independence premise is imported. |
| Liu–Courtade–Cuff–Verdú, *Information-Theoretic Perspectives on Brascamp–Lieb Inequality and Its Reverse*, [arXiv:1702.06260v3, §V-B, Proposition 9][LCCV] | Tensorization uses fixed product reference measures/channels and relative-entropy chain rules. This is a proof pattern; it does not directly cover support-dependent native hard maps. Lemmas 3.1–3.2 discharge that extra step. |
| Wang–Gohari, *Ribbons from Independence Structure: Hypercontractivity, $\Phi$-Mutual Information, and Matrix $\Phi$-Entropy*, [arXiv:2601.18516v1, §§1–3][WG] | Its ribbon bounds depend on specified independent subcollections. Native template laws may be arbitrarily correlated; no such independence is supplied here, and no native cofinality follows from those bounds. |
| Gaubert–Stott, *A convergent hierarchy of non-linear eigenproblems to compute the joint spectral radius of nonnegative matrices*, [arXiv:1805.03284v1, Theorems 3 and 7][GS] | The approximation factor uses a finite family of fixed-size nonnegative matrices and positive irreducibility. No two-direction representation of arbitrary native weighted templates by those matrix products is proved here, so its effective convergence is not transferred. |

